---

<AlternativeLayout
  title="Microsoft Money Alternative & Replacement | MoneyMatter"
  description="Open your Microsoft Money .mny file in MoneyMatter, an open-source replacement you can self-host. Accounts, categories, payees and transfers come across."
  competitor="Microsoft Money"
  heading="An open-source replacement for Microsoft Money"
  intro="MoneyMatter reads Microsoft Money .mny files directly, including password-protected ones. Your accounts, categories, payees, splits and transfers come across. Try the cloud free for 40 days with no card, or host it yourself for free."
  checkedOn={checkedOn}
  atAGlance={AT_A_GLANCE}
  highlights={HIGHLIGHTS}
  comparison={COMPARISON}
  importGuideUrl={DOCS_IMPORT_URL}
  steps={STEPS}
  screenshot={{
    name: 'import-sources',
    width: 1344,
    height: 1082,
    alt: 'MoneyMatter import options, with Microsoft Money listed under From other apps',
  }}
  imported={IMPORTED}
  importLimits={IMPORT_LIMITS}
  faq={FAQ}
  betterFit={STAY_ON_MONEY}
  comparisonNote={`Rows from Status to Support were checked on ${checkedOn} against the sources at the end of this page. Rows from Budgets down describe Money Plus Deluxe and Premium, the 2008 versions that Money Plus Sunset replaces, from our own knowledge of the program, and are not checked against a linked source.`}
  trademarkNote="Microsoft and Microsoft Money are trademarks of the Microsoft group of companies; MoneyMatter is not affiliated with Microsoft."
  sources={SOURCES}
  whyCloud={{ heading: 'Cloud or your own server: what differs', items: WHY_CLOUD }}
>
  <Fragment slot="why-cloud-intro">
    The self-hosted app is the same app with every feature on, and it stays free. The cloud is for people who would
    rather not run a server.
  </Fragment>
</AlternativeLayout>
